From: thingino <thingino@opensensor>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2_jz: add an optional, opt-in probe delay

Adds CONFIG_USB_JZ_DWC2_PROBE_DELAY_MS (int, default 0), and a
msleep() of that many ms at the very start of dwc2_jz_probe().

Default is 0, which makes msleep() a no-op -- zero behavior change for
every board that doesn't explicitly set this. It exists for boards where
CONFIG_USB_JZ_DWC2=y (built into the kernel, probing during early boot,
well under 1 second in) but the USB device wired to this controller is
an internally-powered module (e.g. an LTE modem) whose own power-on
sequencing is independent of and can lag behind the SoC's boot.

Motivating case: Cinnado B6 T23ZN/TM18NA. Stock firmware loads dwc2 as a
loadable module via `insmod` from rcS, which only runs several seconds
into boot (after rootfs mount, hostname setup, etc) -- and the modem
enumerates reliably there. Under Thingino, CONFIG_USB_JZ_DWC2=y probes
at ~0.15s into kernel boot; the modem never enumerates. This gives
boards in that situation a way to approximate stock's timing without
switching the whole driver to loadable-module (and needing a new insmod
script + init ordering to match), while leaving every other board's
boot timing completely unaffected.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/Kconfig b/drivers/usb/dwc2/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/Kconfig
@@ -8,6 +8,16 @@ config USB_JZ_DWC2
 	  If you choose to build this driver is a dynamically linked
 	  module, the module will be called dwc2.ko.
 
+config USB_JZ_DWC2_PROBE_DELAY_MS
+	int "Delay (ms) before dwc2 probe runs"
+	depends on USB_JZ_DWC2
+	default 0
+	help
+	  Sleep this many milliseconds at the very start of dwc2_jz_probe(),
+	  before touching any hardware. 0 (the default) is a no-op. Only
+	  needed on boards with an internally-wired USB device whose own
+	  power-on sequencing can lag noticeably behind SoC boot.
+
 if USB_JZ_DWC2
 
 choice
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/dwc2_jz.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/dwc2_jz.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/dwc2_jz.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/dwc2_jz.c
@@ -487,6 +487,9 @@ static int dwc2_jz_probe(struct platform_device *pdev) {
 	bool init_power_off = false;
 
 	printk(KERN_DEBUG"dwc2 otg probe start\n");
+	if (CONFIG_USB_JZ_DWC2_PROBE_DELAY_MS > 0)
+		msleep(CONFIG_USB_JZ_DWC2_PROBE_DELAY_MS);
+
 	jz = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*jz), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!jz) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "not enough memory\n");
